{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Ice Hockey Puck Wild\n\nOpen the HTML file beside this folder. It is the distributable game. Internet access loads pinned Three.js r180 and Rapier 0.19.3 modules, plus optional display fonts; no server is necessary for solo, couch or direct-link play.\n\n## Play\n\nThree 45-second periods of two-skater arcade hockey, with automatic goalies and sudden death on a tie. Skills Club teaches all five core actions. Three passes charge the team's Wild Shot. The title starts an AI exhibition after ten idle seconds; any input returns to the menu.\n\n- Controller: left stick skate, right stick aim, Cross pass, hold Square or R2 then release to shoot, Circle check, L1 switch, R1 boost, Options pause. Xbox prompts are available in settings.\n- Keyboard: WASD skate, mouse aim, E / right mouse pass, hold Space / left mouse then release to shoot, F check, Q switch, Shift boost, Esc pause.\n- Couch player 2: arrows skate, J shoot, K pass, L check, U switch, O boost. Two standard gamepads also work.\n- Touch: invisible left stick; drag on the right to aim and release to shoot or check. Tap right to pass. Full movement boosts. Only the menu button and contact-sensitive hints appear.\n\nPause → Developer rink provides live skating, shooting, AI, drag, period, check-range and simulation-speed sliders, reset defaults, puck delivery, stamina / Wild Shot refill, score adjustments, period advance, face-off reset and match finish.\n\n## Multiplayer\n\nAI Hub: protocol-v1 shared-world host authority, two seats. The exact Hub client is embedded first in the document head. Host updates the physics and sends snapshots; guests send inputs. A playerless server is supported. No title or extra start confirmation appears in a Hub round.\n\nStandalone two-device play: Friend menu → Direct link. Host creates and shares the invite, guest accepts it and shares the answer, host accepts the answer. Codes carry WebRTC connection descriptions. A STUN server assists address discovery. No TURN relay is included, so restrictive NAT/firewall combinations may prevent the connection.\n\nSame-browser play: Friend menu → Local browser room. Open the same game twice on the same origin, host in one tab and join the six-character room in the other. BroadcastChannel is local to that browser/origin. A localhost server can make same-origin behavior more consistent than file URLs.\n\n## Development\n\nSource modules are deliberately small and editable: \"'`physics.js` owns fixed-step Rapier simulation, `visuals.js` owns the procedural Three.js scene and native animation clips, `audio.js` owns synthesis, `network.js` owns transports, and `game.js` owns input, UI and lifecycle. No generated art or sound files are needed by the game.\n\nRebuild: `python3 build.py` (writes the distributable HTML in the parent folder). `write-metadata.py` writes About/feedback data and the root `exit-interview.json`; run it before rebuilding after metadata changes.\n\nVerify everything with one command from this folder: `./test`. It prints only failures and one total. Tests use the already installed Playwright Python, ephemeral loopback servers and their own browser processes; no shared ports/processes are changed. The suite covers core physics and full shortened match/skills playthroughs, audio samples, mocked-standard gamepad and touch input, settings/menus/attract mode, real two-page WebRTC/BroadcastChannel traffic, the official AI Hub conformance harness, and file-URL packaging. Visual inspection screenshots use the explicit `?webgl=1` compatibility renderer because headless WebGPU screenshots can be blank on this workstation.\n\nReal controller hardware, real touch hardware, iOS Safari and cross-NAT internet behavior remain unconfirmed. Runtime defaults use WebGPU; the renderer can fall back to WebGL compatibility on unsupported browsers.\nEOF\ncat > Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/test <<'\"'EOF'\n#\"'!/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\n\"\"\"One command for the full game verification, with quiet output.\"\"\"\nimport importlib.util\nimport pathlib\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n\ndef package_checks():\n    count=0;failures=[]\n    def check(name,value):\n        nonlocal count\n        count+=1\n        if not value:failures.append(name)\n    try:\n        html=ROOT.parent/(ROOT.name+'\"'.html')\n        raw=html.read_text()\n        info=json.loads((ROOT.parent/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\n        check('single-file deliverable exists and is substantial',len(raw)>100000)\n        check('exact technology versions pinned','three@0.180.0' in raw and 'rapier3d-compat@0.19.3' in raw)\n        check('no local runtime module imports',\\\"from './\\\" not in raw and 'src=\\\"./' not in raw)\n        check('session client placed before other scripts',raw.index('AIHub')<raw.index('type=\\\"importmap\\\"'))\n        check('exit interview complete',list(info)==['sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'] and len(info['sourceInformation'])==15 and len(info['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(info['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(info['promptFeedback'])==4)\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\n            browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'])\n            page=browser.new_page(ignore_https_errors=True)\n            errors=[];page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n            page.goto(html.as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__gameReady',timeout=90000)\n            check('file URL boots the real game',page.title()=='Ice Hockey Puck Wild' and page.evaluate('__game.view.backend===\\\"WebGPU\\\"'))\n            check('in-game credits match root interview',page.evaluate('JSON.stringify(__game.interview)')==json.dumps(info,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':')))\n            check('players use native Three.js animation mixers',page.evaluate('__game.view.players.size===6&&[...__game.view.players.values()].every(p=>p.mixer&&p.mixer._actions.length>=2)'))\n            report=page.evaluate('__game.audioAudit()')\n            check('synthesized audio produces sound',report['rms']>.001)\n            check('synthesized audio samples finite',report['finite'])\n            check('synthesized audio avoids clipping',0<report['peak']<=1)\n            check('music default is ten percent',report['musicDefault']==.1)\n            check('code-written voice synthesis runs',report['stats']['voices']>0)\n            check('code-written effect synthesis runs',report['stats']['sfx']>=4)\n            check('no file-URL runtime errors',not errors)\n            browser.close()\n    except Exception as e:failures.append('packaging/audio: '+str(e).splitlines()[0])\n    return count,failures\n\ncount=0;failures=[];results={}\nfor filename,function in [('test-core.py','check_core'),('test-network.py','check_network'),('test-ui.py','check_ui'),('test-hub.py','check_hub')]:\n    try:\n        spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(filename.replace('-','_'),ROOT/filename)\n        module=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n        checks,problems=getattr(module,function)()\n    except Exception as error:checks,problems=0,[str(error).splitlines()[0]]\n    count+=checks;failures.extend(filename+': '+f for f in problems)\n    results[filename]={'checks':checks,'failures':problems}\nchecks,problems=package_checks();count+=checks;failures.extend(problems);results['packaging/audio']={'checks':checks,'failures':problems}\n(ROOT/'test-results.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks':count,'failures':failures,'suites':results},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor failure in failures:print('FAIL '+failure)\nprint(f'{count} checks; {len(failures)} failures')\nsys.exit(bool(failures))\nEOF\nchmod +x Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/test\ncat Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/audio-audit.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Ice Hockey Puck Wild\n\nOpen the HTML file beside this folder. It is the distributable game. Internet access loads pinned Three.js r180 and Rapier 0.19.3 modules, plus optional display fonts; no server is necessary for solo, couch or direct-link play.\n\n## Play\n\nThree 45-second periods of two-skater arcade hockey, with automatic goalies and sudden death on a tie. Skills Club teaches all five core actions. Three passes charge the team's Wild Shot. The title starts an AI exhibition after ten idle seconds; any input returns to the menu.\n\n- Controller: left stick skate, right stick aim, Cross pass, hold Square or R2 then release to shoot, Circle check, L1 switch, R1 boost, Options pause. Xbox prompts are available in settings.\n- Keyboard: WASD skate, mouse aim, E / right mouse pass, hold Space / left mouse then release to shoot, F check, Q switch, Shift boost, Esc pause.\n- Couch player 2: arrows skate, J shoot, K pass, L check, U switch, O boost. Two standard gamepads also work.\n- Touch: invisible left stick; drag on the right to aim and release to shoot or check. Tap right to pass. Full movement boosts. Only the menu button and contact-sensitive hints appear.\n\nPause → Developer rink provides live skating, shooting, AI, drag, period, check-range and simulation-speed sliders, reset defaults, puck delivery, stamina / Wild Shot refill, score adjustments, period advance, face-off reset and match finish.\n\n## Multiplayer\n\nAI Hub: protocol-v1 shared-world host authority, two seats. The exact Hub client is embedded first in the document head. Host updates the physics and sends snapshots; guests send inputs. A playerless server is supported. No title or extra start confirmation appears in a Hub round.\n\nStandalone two-device play: Friend menu → Direct link. Host creates and shares the invite, guest accepts it and shares the answer, host accepts the answer. Codes carry WebRTC connection descriptions. A STUN server assists address discovery. No TURN relay is included, so restrictive NAT/firewall combinations may prevent the connection.\n\nSame-browser play: Friend menu → Local browser room. Open the same game twice on the same origin, host in one tab and join the six-character room in the other. BroadcastChannel is local to that browser/origin. A localhost server can make same-origin behavior more consistent than file URLs.\n\n## Development\n\nSource modules are deliberately small and editable: \"'`physics.js` owns fixed-step Rapier simulation, `visuals.js` owns the procedural Three.js scene and native animation clips, `audio.js` owns synthesis, `network.js` owns transports, and `game.js` owns input, UI and lifecycle. No generated art or sound files are needed by the game.\n\nRebuild: `python3 build.py` (writes the distributable HTML in the parent folder). `write-metadata.py` writes About/feedback data and the root `exit-interview.json`; run it before rebuilding after metadata changes.\n\nVerify everything with one command from this folder: `./test`. It prints only failures and one total. Tests use the already installed Playwright Python, ephemeral loopback servers and their own browser processes; no shared ports/processes are changed. The suite covers core physics and full shortened match/skills playthroughs, audio samples, mocked-standard gamepad and touch input, settings/menus/attract mode, real two-page WebRTC/BroadcastChannel traffic, the official AI Hub conformance harness, and file-URL packaging. Visual inspection screenshots use the explicit `?webgl=1` compatibility renderer because headless WebGPU screenshots can be blank on this workstation.\n\nReal controller hardware, real touch hardware, iOS Safari and cross-NAT internet behavior remain unconfirmed. Runtime defaults use WebGPU; the renderer can fall back to WebGL compatibility on unsupported browsers.\nEOF\ncat > Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/test <<'\"'EOF'\n#\"'!/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python\n\"\"\"One command for the full game verification, with quiet output.\"\"\"\nimport importlib.util\nimport pathlib\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nROOT=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n\ndef package_checks():\n    count=0;failures=[]\n    def check(name,value):\n        nonlocal count\n        count+=1\n        if not value:failures.append(name)\n    try:\n        html=ROOT.parent/(ROOT.name+'\"'.html')\n        raw=html.read_text()\n        info=json.loads((ROOT.parent/'exit-interview.json').read_text())\n        check('single-file deliverable exists and is substantial',len(raw)>100000)\n        check('exact technology versions pinned','three@0.180.0' in raw and 'rapier3d-compat@0.19.3' in raw)\n        check('no local runtime module imports',\\\"from './\\\" not in raw and 'src=\\\"./' not in raw)\n        check('session client placed before other scripts',raw.index('AIHub')<raw.index('type=\\\"importmap\\\"'))\n        check('exit interview complete',list(info)==['sourceInformation','testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback','aiHub'] and len(info['sourceInformation'])==15 and len(info['testingFeedback'])==4 and len(info['engineFeedback'])==6 and len(info['promptFeedback'])==4)\n        with sync_playwright() as p:\n            browser=p.chromium.launch(headless=True,args=['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader'])\n            page=browser.new_page(ignore_https_errors=True)\n            errors=[];page.on('pageerror',lambda e:errors.append(str(e)))\n            page.goto(html.as_uri());page.wait_for_function('window.__gameReady',timeout=90000)\n            check('file URL boots the real game',page.title()=='Ice Hockey Puck Wild' and page.evaluate('__game.view.backend===\\\"WebGPU\\\"'))\n            check('in-game credits match root interview',page.evaluate('JSON.stringify(__game.interview)')==json.dumps(info,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':')))\n            check('players use native Three.js animation mixers',page.evaluate('__game.view.players.size===6&&[...__game.view.players.values()].every(p=>p.mixer&&p.mixer._actions.length>=2)'))\n            report=page.evaluate('__game.audioAudit()')\n            check('synthesized audio produces sound',report['rms']>.001)\n            check('synthesized audio samples finite',report['finite'])\n            check('synthesized audio avoids clipping',0<report['peak']<=1)\n            check('music default is ten percent',report['musicDefault']==.1)\n            check('code-written voice synthesis runs',report['stats']['voices']>0)\n            check('code-written effect synthesis runs',report['stats']['sfx']>=4)\n            check('no file-URL runtime errors',not errors)\n            browser.close()\n    except Exception as e:failures.append('packaging/audio: '+str(e).splitlines()[0])\n    return count,failures\n\ncount=0;failures=[];results={}\nfor filename,function in [('test-core.py','check_core'),('test-network.py','check_network'),('test-ui.py','check_ui'),('test-hub.py','check_hub')]:\n    try:\n        spec=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(filename.replace('-','_'),ROOT/filename)\n        module=importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec);spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n        checks,problems=getattr(module,function)()\n    except Exception as error:checks,problems=0,[str(error).splitlines()[0]]\n    count+=checks;failures.extend(filename+': '+f for f in problems)\n    results[filename]={'checks':checks,'failures':problems}\nchecks,problems=package_checks();count+=checks;failures.extend(problems);results['packaging/audio']={'checks':checks,'failures':problems}\n(ROOT/'test-results.json').write_text(json.dumps({'checks':count,'failures':failures,'suites':results},indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nfor failure in failures:print('FAIL '+failure)\nprint(f'{count} checks; {len(failures)} failures')\nsys.exit(bool(failures))\nEOF\nchmod +x Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/test\ncat Ice-Hockey-Puck-Wild-Ice-Hockey-1981-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-215207/audio-audit.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"supported\": true,\n  \"finite\": true,\n  \"rms\": 0.018380285541041166,\n  \"peak\": 0.1933588832616806,\n  \"samples\": 132300,\n  \"stats\": {\n    \"tones\": 59,\n    \"noises\": 4,\n    \"voices\": 1,\n    \"musicNotes\": 33,\n    \"effects\": 4\n  },\n  \"musicDefault\": 0.1\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
